    "type": "question",
    "label": "62",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following.\n$$\\frac{4a^7b^2}{8a^9b^5}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{1}{2a^2b^3}$, $a,b\\ne0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{4a^7b^2}{8a^9b^5}&=\\frac12a^{7-9}b^{2-5}\\\\\\frac{4a^7b^2}{8a^9b^5}&=\\frac12a^{-2}b^{-3}\\\\\\frac{4a^7b^2}{8a^9b^5}&=\\frac{1}{2a^2b^3}\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominator requires $a,b\\ne0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
